## "Did you know" tips on the loading screen. <b>, <del> and <key> mark bold, struck and keycap runs.

loading-tip-1 = Pick light or dark theme in Appearance Settings.
loading-tip-2 = Turn off animations with Reduced Motion in Accessibility Settings.
loading-tip-3 = Change Text-to-Speech speed in Accessibility Settings.
loading-tip-4 = Make images accessible to everyone. Add a description on upload.
loading-tip-5 = Make roles with unique colors easier to read in Accessibility Settings.
loading-tip-6 = No mouse? Use Keyboard Mode to get around. <key>tab</key> to get started.
loading-tip-7 = Adjust color saturation in Accessibility Settings.
loading-tip-8 = Jump to different sections of Requiem with <key>f6</key>. <key>tab</key> to get started.
loading-tip-9 = Scale chat font size in Accessibility Settings.
loading-tip-10 = No keyboard? Enable the Send Message button in Appearance Settings to chat.
loading-tip-11 = Discord was almost called Bonfire before we picked our name. It was meant to be nice and cozy.
loading-tip-12 = Discord was almost called Wyvern before we picked our name. Not too proud of that one.
loading-tip-13 = There are a bunch of hidden "Easter Eggs" in the app that happen when you click certain things...
loading-tip-14 = Discord started as a game company making a mobile game called Fates Forever.
loading-tip-15 = Discord’s official birthday is May 13, 2015.
loading-tip-16 = We came up with the idea of Discord Nitro over morning breakfast potatoes.
loading-tip-17 = Our mascot, Wumpus, was originally created as a character with no friends :(
loading-tip-18 = In Discord's early days, light theme was the only theme. Dark theme didn't arrive until August 2015.
loading-tip-19 = In the ancient days, Discord started as a browser-only app.
loading-tip-20 = The character on our 404 page is a robot hamster named Nelly.
loading-tip-21 = You can play our version of the Snake game on our 404 page by pressing a <del>secret</del> button.
loading-tip-22 = There's a very small—and we mean small—chance you can get a secret ringtone when calling someone. Good luck!
loading-tip-23 = Our old Partner mascot was an elf named Springle. He recently retired.
loading-tip-24 = You can use Streamer Mode to hide personal details while streaming.
loading-tip-25 = You can type /tableflip and /unflip to spice up your messages.
loading-tip-26 = Characters like @, #, !, and * will narrow Quick Switcher results.
loading-tip-27 = Click a server name in the emoji picker to hide that server's emoji.
loading-tip-28 = Hover a GIF and click the star to save it to your favorites.
loading-tip-29 = The top-most role for a user defines that user's color.
loading-tip-30 = A red mic icon means that person has been muted by a server admin.
loading-tip-31 = You can temporarily mute a server or channel by right-clicking it.
loading-tip-32 = Click your avatar in the lower-left corner to set a custom status.
loading-tip-33 = Group DMs can have up to ten members.
loading-tip-34 = Click the compass in your server list to find new servers.
loading-tip-35 = Drag and drop servers on top of each other to create server folders.
loading-tip-36 = Type /gif + anything to find a GIF for that topic!
loading-tip-37 = Share what you're playing by using the Game Activity settings.
loading-tip-38 = Highlight text in your chat bar to bold, use italics, and more.
loading-tip-39 = Hide muted channels in a server by right clicking the server name.
loading-tip-40 = Customize Requiem's appearance in the user settings menu.
loading-tip-41 = Link your favorite social media accounts in the connections settings.
loading-tip-42 = You can create channel categories to group and organize your channels.
loading-tip-43 = You can join up to 100 servers, and up to 200 with Nitro!
loading-tip-44 = You can drag and drop files onto Requiem to upload them.
loading-tip-45 = Change each participant's volume by right-clicking them in a call.
loading-tip-46 = Right click to pin messages in a channel or DM to save them for later.
loading-tip-47 = Type a plus sign before an emoji name to turn it into a reaction.
loading-tip-48 = You can type /nick to quickly change your nickname in a server.
loading-tip-49 = You can type / to view bot commands and other built-in commands
loading-tip-50 = You can type ** around your words to make them <b>bold</b>.
loading-tip-51 = <key>mod+k</key> to quickly find a previous conversation or channel.
loading-tip-52 = <key>alt+click</key> a message to mark it as unread.
loading-tip-53 = <key>shift+esc</key> to mark an entire server as read.
loading-tip-54 = <key>shift+alt+up</key> or <key>down</key> will navigate between unread channels
loading-tip-55 = Use <key>mod+/</key> to bring up the list of keyboard shortcuts.
loading-tip-56 = <key>shift+return</key> to make a new line without sending your message.
loading-tip-57 = Holding <key>shift</key> while clicking emoji allows you to send multiple emoji.
loading-tip-58 = You can press <key>up</key> to quickly edit your most recent message.
loading-tip-59 = Statistically speaking, the majority of Discord users believe that pineapple and pizza is the most cursed food combo. Thank our Polls feature launch for this Discord Fact™.
